1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,270
Listen to a talk in a business class.

2
00:00:03,270 --> 00:00:11,130
Today, we're examining the concept of disruptive innovation, a term coined by Clayton Christensen.

3
00:00:11,130 --> 00:00:16,671
Disruptive innovation refers to a process by which a smaller company with fewer resources

4
00:00:16,671 --> 00:00:19,100
successfully challenges established businesses.

5
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:25,002
This typically happens by targeting overlooked segments of the market, offering simpler, cheaper

6
00:00:25,002 --> 00:00:30,020
or more convenient products that eventually appeal to a broader audience.

7
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:34,130
One classic example is the rise of digital photography.

8
00:00:34,130 --> 00:00:38,190
Traditional film-based companies dominated the market for decades.

9
00:00:38,190 --> 00:00:46,010
However, digital cameras initially targeted amateur photographers and offered a new convenient way to take pictures.

10
00:00:46,010 --> 00:00:53,110
Over time, as technology improved, digital photography appealed to professional photographers and everyday consumers

11
00:00:53,110 --> 00:00:58,050
drastically changing the industry and leading to the decline of film companies.

12
00:00:58,050 --> 00:01:03,581
Another example is streaming movie services, some of which started as DVD rental services

13
00:01:03,581 --> 00:01:05,210
that mailed movies to customers.

14
00:01:05,210 --> 00:01:10,070
They disrupted the video rental industry by focusing on consumer convenience.

15
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:16,090
Then as broadband internet became more widespread, they adapted by introducing streaming services

16
00:01:16,090 --> 00:01:21,250
further disrupting established brick-and-mortar businesses that rented DVDs and videotapes.

17
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:26,068
Disruptive innovation often requires companies to rethink their business models

18
00:01:26,068 --> 00:01:29,120
and adapt to changing market conditions.

19
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:35,010
Established businesses might fail to recognize the threat from new entrants until it's too late.

20
00:01:35,010 --> 00:01:39,773
Understanding disruptive innovation is crucial for businesses that want to avoid complacency

21
00:01:39,773 --> 00:01:43,150
and stay competitive in a rapidly evolving marketplace.
